---
import { Font } from 'astro:assets';
import Bare from '../../layouts/Bare.astro';
import { STATIONS } from './_stations';
---

<Bare
  title="As the light flies"
  description="Thirty-four cloud data centres, a stopwatch, and the speed of light in glass: enough to say roughly where on Earth you are, without asking."
>
  <Font cssVariable="--font-alf" slot="head" />

  <main class="alf" data-state="idle">
    <section class="figure" aria-label="Figure 1: the globe">
      <div class="stage">
        <canvas class="globe" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
        <div class="labels" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="marker best" aria-hidden="true" hidden><span>best fit</span></div>
        <div class="marker probe" aria-hidden="true" hidden></div>
        <div class="marker truth" aria-hidden="true" hidden><span>Here</span></div>
        <p class="clock" aria-hidden="true" hidden>
          <span class="clock-t"><i>t</i> = <b>0.0</b> ms</span>
          <span class="clock-d">time for light to go <b>0</b> km and back</span>
        </p>
        <p class="fallback" hidden>This figure needs WebGL 2, which this browser doesn't offer.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="zoom" role="group" aria-label="Zoom">
        <button type="button" data-zoom="in" aria-label="Zoom in">+</button>
        <button type="button" data-zoom="out" aria-label="Zoom out">−</button>
      </div>
      <p class="caption">
        <b>Fig. 1.</b> The Earth, with each region’s limit drawn as its reply comes in. Drag to turn it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="text">
      <header>
        <a class="home" href="/">thesandbox.page</a>
        <h1>As the light flies</h1>
        <p class="deck">
          Light in glass covers about 200 km a millisecond. A server that answers you in 20 ms, there and back, can’t be
          more than 2,000 km away. Ask thirty-four of them at once, and the places their answers allow overlap on one
          patch of the Earth.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="controls">
        <button type="button" class="go">Time the replies</button>
        <button type="button" class="pretend">Pretend you’re elsewhere</button>
      </div>

      <div class="readout" aria-live="polite">
        <p class="lead">Thirty-four regions are waiting on the globe. Nobody has asked them anything yet.</p>
        <p class="detail">
          Your browser will send a few tiny requests to each of Amazon’s cloud regions. They see your address, as any
          site does. The timings stay here.
        </p>
        <p class="actions" hidden>
          <button type="button" class="again">Time them again</button>
          <button type="button" class="locate">Check against where I am</button>
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure class="chart">
        <svg class="plot" viewBox="0 0 400 220" role="img" aria-label="Round trip against distance for every reply"
        ></svg>
        <figcaption>
          <b>Fig. 2.</b> Each reply against its region’s distance from the marked spot. Nothing falls below the line of
          light; over the right spot, the replies line up.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="notes" aria-labelledby="how">
      <h2 id="how">How it works</h2>
      <div class="cols">
        <div>
          <h3>Light in glass</h3>
          <p>
            Signals cross the world as light in optical fibre, which slows it to about two thirds of its speed in a
            vacuum: roughly 200 km every millisecond. A round trip has to go there and back, so each millisecond of reply
            allows at most 100 km between you and the server. Nothing in a reply can make it come back sooner.
          </p>
          <p class="eq"><i>d</i> ≤ ½ · <i>t</i> · ⅔<i>c</i> ≈ <i>t</i> × 100 km/ms</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Circles that must overlap</h3>
          <p>
            Every reply draws a circle around its region that you have to be inside. Thirty-four circles leave only the
            places inside all of them. Turning delays into circles like this is constraint-based geolocation, set out by
            Gueye, Ziviani, Crovella, and Fdida in 2004. Measuring from 42 known points in Western Europe and 95 in the
            United States, they placed hosts to a median of under 25 km and under 100 km.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Slower than light</h3>
          <p>
            Real replies are slower. Cables follow coasts and meet at exchanges, and part of every reply is spent at your
            end: your Wi-Fi, your provider’s first hops, the server’s moment to answer. So for every spot on the globe the
            page fits a line, a shared delay plus so many milliseconds per kilometre, and keeps the spot where the replies
            sit closest along it, counting slow outliers for less, since a detour only ever adds time.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Where it goes wrong</h3>
          <p>
            A VPN or a work network starts your line somewhere else, and the page will find that place instead. Regions
            are sparse across Africa, central Asia, and the Pacific, so the circles there are wide. And each region is
            placed at the city it is named for; the buildings may be some tens of kilometres away.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3 class="ledger-title">The replies</h3>
      <ol class="ledger">
        {
          STATIONS.map((s) => (
            <li data-id={s.id}>
              <span class="where">
                {s.name}
                <small>{s.where}</small>
              </span>
              <span class="rtt">–</span>
              <span class="km">–</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
      <p class="credits">
        Land from Natural Earth, through world-atlas. The regions answer a health check that Amazon keeps open to any
        page; nothing else is asked of them. Set in STIX Two Text.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Bare>

<style is:global>
  body:has(.alf) {
    margin: 0;
    background: #f3f2ee;
  }

  .alf {
    --paper: #f3f2ee;
    --ink: #1b2130;
    --ink-2: #565d6c;
    --ink-3: #8a8f99;
    --rule: #cfcdc6;
    --cobalt: #2a55c9;
    --vermilion: #d9432a;
    --serif: var(--font-alf), Cambria, Georgia, serif;

    box-sizing: border-box;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(330px, 420px);
    grid-template-areas:
      'figure text'
      'notes notes';
    min-height: 100vh;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.45;
    font-variant-numeric: lining-nums tabular-nums;
  }

  .alf *,
  .alf *::before,
  .alf *::after {
    box-sizing: inherit;
  }

  .alf [hidden] {
    display: none !important;
  }

  .alf button {
    font: inherit;
    color: inherit;
  }

  .alf .figure {
    grid-area: figure;
    position: relative;
    height: 100vh;
    min-height: 560px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-rows: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    padding: 24px 0 18px 28px;
  }

  .alf .stage {
    position: relative;
    min-height: 0;
    touch-action: none;
    cursor: grab;
  }

  .alf .stage.dragging {
    cursor: grabbing;
  }

  .alf .globe {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }

  .alf .labels {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .alf .st {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.3em;
    white-space: nowrap;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--ink);
    transform: translate(var(--x), var(--y));
    transition: opacity 0.25s;
  }

  .alf .st b {
    font-weight: 500;
    font-variant-caps: all-small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    font-size: 1.12em;
  }

  .alf .st em {
    font-style: normal;
    color: var(--cobalt);
  }

  .alf .marker {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    width: 0;
    height: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    transform: translate(var(--x), var(--y));
  }

  .alf .probe::before,
  .alf .probe::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    background: var(--ink);
  }

  .alf .probe::before {
    left: -9px;
    top: -0.5px;
    width: 18px;
    height: 1px;
  }

  .alf .probe::after {
    left: -0.5px;
    top: -9px;
    width: 1px;
    height: 18px;
  }

  .alf .truth::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: -5px;
    top: -5px;
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--ink);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--paper);
  }

  .alf .truth span {
    position: absolute;
    left: 9px;
    top: 4px;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-style: italic;
    white-space: nowrap;
    text-shadow:
      0 0 3px var(--paper),
      0 0 3px var(--paper);
  }

  .alf .best::before,
  .alf .best::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    background: var(--vermilion);
  }

  .alf .best::before {
    left: -11px;
    top: -1px;
    width: 22px;
    height: 2px;
  }

  .alf .best::after {
    left: -1px;
    top: -11px;
    width: 2px;
    height: 22px;
  }

  .alf .best span {
    position: absolute;
    right: 10px;
    bottom: 5px;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--vermilion);
    white-space: nowrap;
    text-shadow:
      0 0 3px var(--paper),
      0 0 3px var(--paper),
      0 0 2px var(--paper);
  }

  .alf .clock {
    position: absolute;
    left: 10px;
    bottom: 10px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 8px 14px 10px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 2px;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    background: rgb(243 242 238 / 0.9);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 3px;
  }

  .alf .clock-t {
    font-size: 26px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .alf .clock b {
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .alf .fallback {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 40% 10% auto;
    text-align: center;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .alf .zoom {
    position: absolute;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 56px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 6px;
  }

  .alf .zoom button {
    width: 34px;
    height: 34px;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--paper);
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .alf .zoom button:hover {
    border-color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .alf .caption {
    margin: 10px 0 0;
    max-width: 46em;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .alf .caption b,
  .alf figcaption b {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .alf .text {
    grid-area: text;
    padding: 26px 36px 20px 28px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
    max-height: 100vh;
    min-height: 560px;
    overflow: auto;
  }

  .alf header {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .alf .home {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    text-decoration: none;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .alf .home:hover {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .alf h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 46px;
    line-height: 1;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: italic;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .alf .deck {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 16.5px;
  }

  .alf .controls {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .alf .controls button,
  .alf .actions button {
    padding: 9px 16px 10px;
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: transparent;
    font-size: 16px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .alf .controls .go {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  .alf .controls .go:hover {
    background: #2e3649;
  }

  .alf .controls .pretend:hover,
  .alf .actions button:hover {
    background: rgb(27 33 48 / 0.06);
  }

  .alf .controls button:disabled,
  .alf .actions button:disabled {
    opacity: 0.4;
    cursor: default;
  }

  .alf .readout {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding-top: 14px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .alf .readout p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .alf .readout .lead {
    font-size: 19.5px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .alf .readout .detail {
    font-size: 15.5px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .alf .readout .detail:empty {
    display: none;
  }

  .alf .actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .alf .actions button {
    padding: 6px 13px 7px;
    font-size: 14.5px;
  }

  .alf .chart {
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 6px;
  }

  .alf .plot {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    overflow: visible;
  }

  .alf figcaption {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .alf .notes {
    grid-area: notes;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    margin: 0 36px 0 28px;
    padding: 30px 0 56px;
  }

  .alf .notes h2 {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    font-size: 30px;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .alf .notes .cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
    gap: 10px 36px;
  }

  .alf .notes h3 {
    margin: 0 0 6px;
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-variant-caps: all-small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }

  .alf .notes p {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    font-size: 16px;
  }

  .alf .notes .eq {
    font-size: 18px;
  }

  .alf .ledger-title {
    margin-top: 28px !important;
  }

  .alf .ledger {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    columns: 3 270px;
    column-gap: 36px;
    font-size: 14.5px;
  }

  .alf .ledger li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 5.2em 6.4em;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 4px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px dotted var(--rule);
    break-inside: avoid;
  }

  .alf .ledger small {
    margin-left: 0.4em;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }

  .alf .ledger .rtt,
  .alf .ledger .km {
    text-align: right;
  }

  .alf .ledger .km {
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .alf .credits {
    margin-top: 24px !important;
    font-size: 13.5px !important;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    /* One column: the globe follows the title, and the text's other parts follow the globe. */
    .alf {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .alf .text {
      display: contents;
    }

    .alf header {
      order: 1;
      padding: 22px 18px 6px;
    }

    .alf .figure {
      order: 2;
      height: auto;
      min-height: 0;
      padding: 0 18px 12px;
      grid-template-rows: auto auto;
    }

    .alf .controls {
      order: 3;
      padding: 0 18px;
    }

    .alf .readout {
      order: 5;
      margin: 16px 18px 0;
    }

    .alf .chart {
      order: 6;
      margin: 18px 18px 26px;
    }

    .alf .notes {
      order: 7;
    }

    .alf .stage {
      aspect-ratio: 1;
    }

    .alf .zoom {
      right: 18px;
      bottom: 60px;
    }

    .alf .notes {
      margin: 0 18px;
    }

    .alf h1 {
      font-size: 38px;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  import { start } from './_app';

  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.alf');
  if (root) start(root);
</script>
